I have a PWS600au with 768MB of RAM and a PIII450 with 512MB RAM. Both are
running FreeBSD 4.7-RELEASE. I noticed that after two weeks uptime my PWS
uses a lot more memory than the PIII (and running the same amount of
programs). At a moment it even used 350MB of swap. The memory usage just
keeps increasing. The intel doesn't do that.

Why is this? Is this a difference between the alpha/intel architecture of
FreeBSD or is it something else?


